  "enhanced_information": "Probenecid is a uricosuric drug that increases uric acid excretion, thereby reducing serum uric acid levels and is used in the treatment of gout. Allopurinol, while effective in lowering uric acid levels, works by inhibiting uric acid production and is not classified as a uricosuric drug. Indomethacin is a non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) used primarily for its anti-inflammatory effects and does not have uricosuric properties. Aspirin can have conflicting effects on uric acid excretion, particularly at low doses, and is not primarily considered a uricosuric drug. Therefore, the only uricosuric drug among the options is Probenecid."
